## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage theater"** — every production method is called (→ 95% coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified. Here's the ranked list:

---

### 🔴 Critical: Missing Assertions (Assert-Free Tests)

**Lines 17–21 (`AddProduct_Works`), 33–35 (`UpdatePrice_Works`), 39–42 (`RemoveProduct_Works`), 64–66 (`GetProductCount_Works`), 68–74 (`ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`), 85–88 (`ImportFromCsv_Works`)**

These tests have **zero assertions**. They only prove the code doesn't throw. Bugs in logic (wrong price saved, item not deleted, discount miscalculated) will never be caught.

**Fixes:**
```csharp
// AddProduct_Works
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);

// UpdatePrice_Works
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);

// RemoveProduct_Works
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));

// GetProductCount_Works
Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());

// ApplyBulkDiscount_Works (10% off)
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);

// ImportFromCsv_Works
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(imported);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);
```

---

### 🟠 High: Weak Assertions (`IsNotNull` on non-nullable paths)

**Lines 28 (`GetProduct_Works`), 51 (`SearchProducts_Works`), 59 (`GetAllProducts_Works`), 81 (`ExportToCsv_Works`)**

`Assert.IsNotNull` verifies the method returned *something* but never checks correctness. `Search("Widget")` could return `["Gadget"]` and pass. `GetAll()` could return 50 duplicates and pass.

**Fixes:**
```csharp
// GetProduct_Works
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);

// SearchProducts_Works
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);

// GetAllProducts_Works
